# Inert until collections-as-call-arguments lands (sub-bindings are numeric-only) — see Future.md. The fold itself is proven equivalent to the C++ reducer (tests.cpp).
# sum_of(xs) — sum of a seq collection, as a foldl over the add operator.
# This is the SPEC definition: it coexists with the C++ `sum` fast-path and is
# proven equivalent to it (see the equivalence proof in src/tests.cpp). Empty
# collection -> 0 (the add identity / fold seed).
@include "add.fw"
[sum_of(xs) -> result]
result = foldl(xs, add, 0)
